msgid "max_autotune 使用示例"
msgstr "max_autotune usage example"

msgid ""
"`max_autotune` 是 Triton-Ascend 提供的增强自动调优装饰器，旨在简化多参数调优的代码编写。与社区版 `autotune` "
"要求用户手动枚举所有 `triton.Config` 不同，`max_autotune` "
"允许用户仅提供少量基础配置（如分块大小），并自动将相关的编译器选项（如 "
"`num_stages`、`enable_hivm_auto_cv_balance` "
"等）纳入最优组合的搜索空间。用户也可以通过参数列表显式控制搜索范围。"
msgstr ""
"`max_autotune` is an enhanced auto-tuning decorator provided by Triton-"
"Ascend, designed to simplify the code writing for multi-parameter tuning. "
"Unlike the community version of `autotune`, which requires users to manually"
" enumerate all `triton.Config` instances, `max_autotune` allows users to "
"provide only a small set of base configurations (such as block sizes) and "
"automatically incorporates related compiler options (such as `num_stages`, "
"`enable_hivm_auto_cv_balance`, etc.) into the search space for optimal "
"combinations. Users can also explicitly control the search scope through a "
"parameter list."

msgid "**适用场景**：Ascend NPU 上的 `cube`、`mix`、`vector` 算子，尤其适合需要同时调整多个硬件相关参数的场景。"
msgstr ""
"**Applicable Scenarios**: `cube`, `mix`, and `vector` operators on Ascend "
"NPU, particularly suitable for scenarios where multiple hardware-related "
"parameters need to be adjusted simultaneously."

msgid "基本使用示例"
msgstr "Basic usage example"

msgid ""
"以下示例演示了使用 `max_autotune` 对一个简单的向量加法 kernel 进行自动调优。与社区版 `autotune` "
"相比，`max_autotune` 还会自动将不同的编译器选项纳入调优空间，无需用户手动指定。"
msgstr ""
"The following example demonstrates automatic tuning of a simple vector "
"addition kernel using `max_autotune`. Compared to the community edition "
"`autotune`, `max_autotune` also automatically includes different compiler "
"options in the tuning space, without requiring users to specify them "
"manually."

msgid ""
"import torch\n"
"import torch_npu\n"
"import triton\n"
"import triton.language as tl\n"
"from triton.backends.ascend.runtime import max_autotune\n"
"\n"
"def test_max_autotune():\n"
"\n"
"    # Basic configuration: only the block size needs to be provided; other tuning parameters are auto-generated by the decorator\n"
"    base_configs = [\n"
"        triton.Config({'BLOCK_SIZE': 128}),\n"
"        triton.Config({'BLOCK_SIZE': 256}),\n"
"    ]\n"
"\n"
"    @max_autotune(\n"
"        configs=base_configs,\n"
"        key=[\"numel\"],\n"
"        kernel_type=\"vector\",          # Kernel type: cube / mix / vector, defaults to mix\n"
"    )\n"
"    @triton.jit\n"
"    def triton_calc_kernel(\n"
"        out_ptr0, in_ptr0, in_ptr1, numel,\n"
"        BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr\n"
"    ):\n"
"        pid = tl.program_id(0)\n"
"        idx = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n"
"        mask = idx < numel\n"
"\n"
"        # Simulate computation load\n"
"        for i in range(10000):\n"
"            tmp0 = tl.load(in_ptr0 + idx, mask=mask, other=0.0)\n"
"            tmp1 = tl.load(in_ptr1 + idx, mask=mask, other=0.0)\n"
"            tmp2 = tl.math.exp(tmp0) + tmp1 + i\n"
"            tl.store(out_ptr0 + idx, tmp2, mask=mask)\n"
"\n"
"    # Wrapper invocation function\n"
"    def triton_calc_func(x0, x1):\n"
"        n = x0.numel()\n"
"        y0 = torch.empty_like(x0)\n"
"        grid = lambda meta: (triton.cdiv(n, meta[\"BLOCK_SIZE\"]),)\n"
"        triton_calc_kernel[grid](y0, x0, x1, n)\n"
"        return y0\n"
"\n"
"    # Compare against the PyTorch reference result\n"
"    def torch_calc_func(x0, x1):\n"
"        return torch.exp(x0) + x1 + 10000 - 1\n"
"\n"
"    DEV = \"npu\"\n"
"    DTYPE = torch.float32\n"
"    N = 192 * 1024\n"
"    x0 = torch.randn((N,), dtype=DTYPE, device=DEV)\n"
"    x1 = torch.randn((N,), dtype=DTYPE, device=DEV)\n"
"    torch_ref = torch_calc_func(x0, x1)\n"
"    triton_cal = triton_calc_func(x0, x1)\n"
"    torch.testing.assert_close(triton_cal, torch_ref)\n"
"\n"
"if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n"
"    test_max_autotune()\n"
"    print(\"success: test_max_autotune\")"
msgstr ""
"import torch\n"
"import torch_npu\n"
"import triton\n"
"import triton.language as tl\n"
"from triton.backends.ascend.runtime import max_autotune\n"
"\n"
"def test_max_autotune():\n"
"\n"
"    # Basic configuration: only the block size needs to be provided; other tuning parameters are auto-generated by the decorator\n"
