msgid "进阶使用：精确控制调优参数"
msgstr "Advanced Usage: Precisely Controlling Tuning Parameters"

msgid ""
"用户可以通过 **tuning_params** "
"显式指定需要调优的编译器选项及其取值列表；未指定的参数会使用内置默认值。以下示例展示了如何对多个参数进行组合搜索。"
msgstr ""
"You can use **tuning_params** to explicitly specify the compiler options for"
" tuning and their lists of values. Parameters that are not specified use "
"built-in default values. The following example shows how to perform a "
"combined search across multiple parameters."

msgid ""
"from triton.backends.ascend.runtime import max_autotune\n"
"\n"
"def test_max_autotune():\n"
"\n"
"    # Basic configuration: only the block size needs to be provided; other tuning parameters are auto-generated by the decorator\n"
"    base_configs = [\n"
"        triton.Config({'BLOCK_SIZE': 128}),\n"
"        triton.Config({'BLOCK_SIZE': 256}),\n"
"    ]\n"
"\n"
"    @max_autotune(\n"
"        configs=base_configs,          # Basic configuration list\n"
"        key=[\"numel\"],                 # Re-trigger tuning when numel changes\n"
"        kernel_type=\"vector\",          # Kernel type: cube / mix / vector\n"
"        # The following parameters are optional tuning lists; built-in defaults are used when not provided\n"
"        num_stages=[1, 2],\n"
"        enable_ubuf_saving=[True, False]\n"
"    )\n"
"    @triton.jit\n"
"    def triton_calc_kernel(\n"
"        out_ptr0, in_ptr0, in_ptr1, numel,\n"
"        BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\n"
"        **META\n"
"    ):\n"
"        pass"
msgstr ""
